sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/empty-shell-morphospace--claude-opus-5-5--3> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Lean-proved constructional boundaries of Raup space plus a growth-rule reachability map" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/empty-shell-morphospace> ;
    dct:description "Separate what geometry forbids outright from what development or selection disfavours. Formalize in Lean the logarithmic-spiral shell: the generating curve's centroid at angle θ is at radius r(θ) = r₀ W^{θ/2π}, with the curve's inner edge at distance proportional to D·r. Prove: (a) successive whorls just touch when D = 1/W, Raup's boundary between overlapping and separated coils, generalized to elliptical generating curves; (b) a whorl penetrates the previous one exactly when D < 1/W under stated conditions, with the conditions on T for helicospiral forms; (c) for T = 0, an umbilicus exists iff D > 0. These carve out the constructionally impossible region (self-intersection), which must not count as an 'unexplained empty region'. Second, derive developmental reachability from local aperture growth rules (Moulton–Goriely style, with growth rate varying around the aperture): compute which (W, D, T) combinations are produced by growth-rate profiles in a bounded family, giving the developmental-constraint surface M_dev for approach 1." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Lean theorems giving the exact self-intersection boundary of Raup space (D = 1/W and its elliptical and helicospiral generalizations), and a growth-rule reachability density. Together they separate 'impossible', 'developmentally unlikely' and 'possible but unoccupied' regions, the three-way distinction the problem needs." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The growth-rule family is so flexible that every geometrically valid point is reachable, leaving M_dev uninformative; or the geometric theorems hold only under circular generating curves, too restrictive for real gastropods." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/mixed" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Define the spiral shell in Lean with ℝ parameters; prove the touching and penetration conditions with explicit hypotheses. 2. Report the theorems against Thompson ch11 claims (logarithmic spiral generative model). 3. Implement an aperture-growth model; sample growth-rate profiles; record resulting (W, D, T). 4. Produce the reachability density as M_dev for approach 1." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): tractable" ;
    skos:note "Tool: lean4" ;
    skos:note "Tool: mathlib" ;
    skos:note "Tool: simulation" ;
    skos:note "Tool: theoretical-morphology" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-09> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-05> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-15> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1301405> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/empty-shell-morphospace> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Why is shell morphospace empty where it is?" .


  <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1301405> dct:bibliographicCitation "Raup 1966, the W = 1/D boundary" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009> dct:title "Mechanical growth and morphogenesis of seashells" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Moulton, Goriely and Chirat 2012, growth-based shell morphogenesis" .
}

